-> ABOUT [node:73fb6132-40d3-4e2d-8b88-334442c4bfa7] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:08.639286+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:dffe0843-23d7-4095-99e1-1d39a07d1b2a] @ 2026-09-08T09:37:37.208429+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-08T09:37:37.208429+00:00

Warn and fail are never amber. They sit at hue 45 and hue 27, visibly hotter and redder than ink amber at hue 72, because on a warm amber screen a warm warning is invisible - the hue separation has to be earned.
