[node:77925b30-350a-42ee-a7de-7e8a023c5708]
type: decision
tier: lifetime
path: /artifact/frontend-is-svelte-5-with-components-exp
created_at: 2026-09-08T09:38:00.559118+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> ABOUT [node:49ba726c-031e-4a01-839f-11a76a8bf009] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:10.816257+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:716987ce-f933-41b5-8c4e-590c09dc33bf] @ 2026-09-08T09:38:00.559118+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:79662ce5-7b55-458a-b0e9-f0efd406d5a8] @ 2026-09-08T09:38:54.460001+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:a1174884-8d33-4260-af5b-0f97264a2ea2] @ 2026-09-08T09:38:00.559118+00:00

Frontend is Svelte 5 with components exported as custom elements rather than hand-written native JS. Svelte compiles away - no virtual DOM, no framework runtime, roughly 2-5 KB gzip against React+ReactDOM's 40-45 KB - so on A8X-class hardware the overhead against plain JS is negligible while the developer experience is far better. Compiling to custom elements satisfies the Web Components requirement, and the hexagonal architecture survives because components are a UI adapter behind a port.
---
