path: /artifact/the-service-worker-aims-at-a-full-offlin
created_at: 2026-09-08T09:38:30.445420+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:0bc7e618-9b95-4977-9fe1-f3a48759276f] @ 2026-09-08T09:38:30.445420+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:15863232-0fb0-4c79-aaa9-3750ce8c0a2f] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:12.574912+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:3c7e1fe3-fba9-48d1-b1f3-8dc9b463a550] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:12.428170+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:a1174884-8d33-4260-af5b-0f97264a2ea2] @ 2026-09-08T09:38:30.445420+00:00

K7's Service Worker (hand-rolled, chosen over workbox, shipped in k7-offline-shell) is scoped to the app shell only today — no API response is cached, so a network outage loses all card data even though the shell repaints. Decided 2026-09-14: selected API responses — calendar first — are to be cached by the Service Worker with a stale-while-revalidate strategy: serve the cached response, revalidate in the background once it is stale, and fall back to the cached version when a fresh fetch is unavailable. Not yet implemented. Which other endpoints qualify (a mutating write path likely does not) and the per-endpoint invalidation details remain open.
---
