[node:36e6377e-7d18-4de2-b827-8644f15bf56a]
type: constraint
tier: lifetime
path: /artifact/context-memory-graph-dump-is-marked-mer
created_at: 2026-09-08T09:55:56.268439+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:a17b142e-850e-4cdb-8d84-2689e75428a7] @ 2026-09-08T09:55:56.268439+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c62c070b-e4a6-41b3-86f3-00ad5d96800f] @ 2026-09-08T09:55:56.268439+00:00

context/memory-graph.dump is marked -merge in .gitattributes so git never line-merges it. Git aligns similar blocks and shows only their differing lines, so a three-way merge of the dump can splice half of one node's entry onto half of another and produce a store that parses and is wrong. The documented recovery, agentic-memory sync resolve, does not exist in the installed CLI - sync accepts only status, dump and restore - so a conflict is resolved by keeping one side whole, running sync restore to rebuild the database from it, and re-capturing whatever the discarded side held.
---
