archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:4c740d82-541d-4c70-9970-793467c4f26e] @ 2026-09-08T11:24:46.150128+00:00
-> CONTRADICTS [node:7835061e-c325-4e70-8051-105f22ff4f8a] @ 2026-09-08T11:24:46.150128+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:7835061e-c325-4e70-8051-105f22ff4f8a] @ 2026-09-08T11:43:43.560365+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c62c070b-e4a6-41b3-86f3-00ad5d96800f] @ 2026-09-08T11:24:46.150128+00:00

The middleware composition library ships as the scoped package @mt3o/middleware-pipe rather than a bare name, because the unscoped middleware-pipe was already taken on npm. Scoping was chosen over inventing a different bare name: it keeps the library's own identity readable, and it ends the naming race for everything else the project may publish. Version 1.0.0 is public from github.com/mt3o/middlewares with publishConfig.access set to public. npm never releases a published name for reuse, so this one is permanent. It clears the first of the two blockers on Faza 0; the empty vidataflux repository is the other.
---
