path: /artifact/the-canonical-theme-carries-two-names-fo
created_at: 2026-09-08T13:42:46.046271+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> ABOUT [node:73fb6132-40d3-4e2d-8b88-334442c4bfa7] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:46.046271+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:46.046271+00:00

The canonical theme carries two names for one colour role: signal is the v2 name and accentSecondary is kept as a v1 alias, with identical values in all three modes. Every consumer that reads accentSecondary works, which is exactly why the alias will outlive the migration unless someone retires it deliberately.
---
[node:0598ee91-68fa-455a-86af-4d5325c91066]
type: issue
tier: mid-term
path: /artifact/slideshow-is-declared-as-an-entry-in-a-l
created_at: 2026-09-08T13:42:46.173590+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> ABOUT [node:49ba726c-031e-4a01-839f-11a76a8bf009] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:46.173590+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:d2844438-9992-4e20-bfb5-fa615a906574] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:46.173590+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:46.173590+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:f96f62c3-d72a-4c40-8e16-57278ca1f302] @ 2026-09-08T13:42:46.173590+00:00

Slideshow is declared as an entry in a layout's card list but the schema then spends a paragraph saying it is not a card: it renders nothing in its own grid slot, its span is ignored, at most one may exist per layout, and it may not be nested in a carousel, a card grid or the sidebar. The type system says card and the semantics say layout controller, so every one of those rules has to be enforced by hand at validation time rather than falling out of the shape.
---
