-> HAS_FACET [node:4c740d82-541d-4c70-9970-793467c4f26e] @ 2026-09-08T15:29:05.877424+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:a815b136-0de2-49af-ac42-6192c12def24] @ 2026-09-08T15:29:16.723149+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:be297a51-6cb1-4526-bdb5-c01badf562a2] @ 2026-09-08T15:29:05.877424+00:00

SQLite opens with journal_mode WAL and foreign_keys ON, and neither is a default. The kiosk reads on a timer while the backend writes, and under the default rollback journal every read waits behind a write - visible on the wall as a stutter. Foreign keys are off per-connection unless asked for, which means a schema full of cascades and set-nulls is decorative until the pragma is set; the persistence tests assert a foreign key violation specifically so that a future connection helper that forgets the pragma fails the build instead of silently discarding referential integrity.
---
