-> ABOUT [node:8b9566f6-a1d5-4c43-952e-369c2796d5ca] @ 2026-09-08T15:29:05.996486+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:be297a51-6cb1-4526-bdb5-c01badf562a2] @ 2026-09-08T15:29:05.996486+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:f2e09a03-8e61-4299-ad7c-cef6c06775fe] @ 2026-09-08T15:29:05.996486+00:00

An AiCall's foreign keys are nullable and delete with set null, while a Message cascades with its Conversation. This is the domain model expressed as a schema rather than a storage convenience: a Message has no identity outside its thread, so deleting the thread should take it, but an AiCall is a record of money spent and a single Message may cost several - compacting spends them with no Message at all. Deleting a conversation must therefore leave its cost history standing, orphaned but intact, because the cost view answers what the household spent and not which threads still exist.
---
