path: /artifact/a-variable-named-state-breaks-every-sta
created_at: 2026-09-09T05:38:22.741693+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:a1174884-8d33-4260-af5b-0f97264a2ea2] @ 2026-09-09T05:38:22.741693+00:00

A variable named state breaks every $state rune in the same Svelte 5 component. The dollar prefix is still store-subscription syntax, so $state parses as a subscription to a local called state, and the compiler reports block-scoped variable used before its declaration pointing at each rune rather than at the name that caused it. The errors name the wrong line, which is what makes it expensive: the fix is renaming the variable, and nothing in the message suggests that. The same collision waits for any local named props, derived or effect.
---
