-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-09T06:55:33.083742+00:00

A date captured once when a component initialises stops being today at the first midnight. On a display that runs for months this is not an edge case but a certainty, and the card it breaks first is the calendar, whose whole job is saying what day it is; the highlighted column silently drifts a day behind and nothing about the failure looks like a failure. Anything that means now must be recomputed on a timer rather than closed over at construction.
