The chat card's params contract (docs/handoff/layout.schema.yaml params.chat, layout.yaml id: czat) already pins ConversationService's budgeting interface before any code exists: defaultModel (required string), optional availableModels (empty = fetch dynamically from GET /api/gateway/models), contextWindowMarginPercent (5-50, default 20, reserved for the response) and compactingThresholdPercent (50-95, default 80, triggers compacting), plus voiceInput (boolean, default false) for the mic feature. These are the exact knobs the service's budgeting/compacting logic must read from card params rather than invent.
