-> HAS_FACET [node:4c740d82-541d-4c70-9970-793467c4f26e] @ 2026-09-09T11:58:41.643681+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:68b03a85-d372-45c5-80a4-549ebf826798] @ 2026-09-09T11:58:41.643681+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:f29aa338-eddb-456b-97ad-00b602cb9a42] @ 2026-09-09T11:58:41.643681+00:00

ConversationService's context-budgeting uses a chars/4 token-count heuristic rather than a real tokenizer (no tiktoken-equivalent dependency added). Chosen because this is a kiosk-scale hobby project — the cost of an occasional misbudget (compacting a turn early/late) is low, and a real tokenizer means picking and pinning one per provider/model family Kilo Gateway fronts, which the gateway itself doesn't disclose. Documented as approximate; the real prompt_tokens/completion_tokens the gateway reports are used for actual cost logging (ai_calls) whenever present, so billing accuracy doesn't depend on the estimate — only the compacting trigger point does.
---
