-> HAS_FACET [node:4c740d82-541d-4c70-9970-793467c4f26e] @ 2026-09-09T12:01:33.517864+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:68b03a85-d372-45c5-80a4-549ebf826798] @ 2026-09-09T12:01:33.517864+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:7b73e502-b1fb-4587-96bd-f005b1ead665] @ 2026-09-09T12:01:33.517864+00:00

ConversationService is implemented as a plain async generator interface — streamTurn(input, signal): AsyncGenerator<ChatEvent> — with zero Fastify/HTTP types anywhere in the module. The SSE route's only job is to iterate the generator and write each ChatEvent as an SSE frame. This is the concrete interface chosen to satisfy the CONVSERVICE constraint (decoupled from the chat HTTP endpoint so MCP/a skill can drive it later): the generator boundary is what makes a future non-HTTP caller (an MCP tool, a CLI skill) able to consume the exact same turn logic by just iterating it, with no adapter needed beyond swapping who reads the events.
---
