-> HAS_FACET [node:4c740d82-541d-4c70-9970-793467c4f26e] @ 2026-09-09T12:04:24.069216+00:00

Node's built-in TypeScript type-stripping (used to run src/server/*.ts directly via `node --watch`/`node --test`, no separate transpile step) does not support TS constructor parameter properties ("constructor(public readonly x: T)") — it throws ERR_UNSUPPORTED_TYPESCRIPT_SYNTAX at runtime even though tsc/svelte-check would accept it. Discovered writing RecipeImportError in src/server/recipes/import.ts; fixed by declaring the field and assigning it in the constructor body instead. Any future server-side class with constructor-shorthand fields will hit the same failure.
