Extending upstreamCache's `upstream` Drizzle enum (and the domain-level Upstream union) needs no migration on SQLite — drizzle-kit generate confirmed "No schema changes, nothing to migrate": SQLite text columns carry no CHECK constraint from a Drizzle enum, it's TS-level only. Plan.md's Phase 1 assumed a migration would be needed; it wasn't. Future Upstream/enum-like additions on this schema can skip the migration step entirely as long as the column stays `text`.
