-> HAS_FACET [node:ccc18558-7181-44df-9608-de587d8d937c] @ 2026-09-10T04:32:29.283797+00:00

Kilo Gateway's POST /api/gateway/audio/transcriptions is a real, distinct route — confirmed live 2026-09-10 via the x-matched-path response header (= /api/gateway/audio/transcriptions), unlike a genuinely unknown path (e.g. /api/gateway/audio/speech) which falls through to the catch-all "This endpoint only accepts the path `/chat/completions`" error. However its exact request contract could NOT be verified: every unauthenticated attempt (JSON body, multipart/form-data body, valid JSON with model+file fields, a fake bearer token) returned the same generic {"error":"Invalid request","error_type":"invalid_request","message":"Could not parse request body. Please ensure it is valid JSON."} before any auth-specific error appeared (contrast: chat/completions with a fake bearer returns a distinct PAID_MODEL_AUTH_REQUIRED error). No real KILO_GATEWAY_KEY is available in this sandbox (secrets are server-side only per project policy), so the field names/shape (multipart vs JSON, field name for the audio payload) remain a documented best-effort assumption — OpenAI-Whisper-style multipart with fields `file` and `model` — not a live-verified contract, unlike the chat-completions shape in upstream/kilo.ts which was fully verified live.
---
