-> HAS_FACET [node:a1174884-8d33-4260-af5b-0f97264a2ea2] @ 2026-09-10T04:39:10.736540+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:d2844438-9992-4e20-bfb5-fa615a906574] @ 2026-09-10T04:39:29.859566+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-10T04:39:10.736540+00:00

Slideshow's fullscreen presentation promotes the already-rendered target card element in place (a CSS class giving it position:fixed; inset:0) rather than reparenting or cloning it. Reparenting a Svelte custom element via appendChild fires disconnectedCallback/connectedCallback, which tears down and remounts the Svelte component instance, losing internal state (a running timer, an armed/streaming audiometer, in-progress chat scroll). In-place CSS promotion works because .pager-track's inline transform is the only ancestor that would otherwise create a new containing block for position:fixed (a transformed ancestor makes fixed descendants position relative to it, not the viewport); the transform is temporarily cleared while the slideshow is active and restored via the existing pager.go() handle on exit.
---
