-> HAS_FACET [node:a1174884-8d33-4260-af5b-0f97264a2ea2] @ 2026-09-10T04:56:18.567508+00:00
-> ABOUT [node:d2844438-9992-4e20-bfb5-fa615a906574] @ 2026-09-10T04:56:18.567508+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-10T04:56:18.567508+00:00

The slideshow's promoted fullscreen card stays a DOM descendant of .pager-track/deck even though it is visually position:fixed — DOM event bubbling follows the tree, not paint position. An independent plan review caught that the page-level pager (pager.ts) was still listening for touchstart/touchmove/touchend on deck and keydown on window with no awareness the slideshow owns the screen, so an interaction meant to exit the slideshow would also be read as a page swipe/arrow-key, silently repainting the pager to the wrong page underneath. Fixed by adding suspend()/resume() to Pager (pager.ts): a `suspended` flag checked at the top of every pager handler, called by the slideshow controller around fullscreen entry/exit. This is a genuine architectural fix, not a documentation note — pager.ts's public Pager interface changed.
---
