-> HAS_FACET [node:a1174884-8d33-4260-af5b-0f97264a2ea2] @ 2026-09-14T19:47:43.360131+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-14T19:47:43.360131+00:00

Do not use the native browser Fullscreen API (Element.requestFullscreen) for card fullscreen on K7. Support on iPadOS 15 Safari — this project's hard device baseline — is inconsistent for arbitrary (non-video) elements: Apple staff have stated on the WebKit developer forums that it should be available on iPadOS, but multiple developers report it silently failing in practice; the `isElementFullscreenEnabled` WKPreferences flag that reliably enables it only exists from iOS/iPadOS 15.4 and macOS 12.3 onward and governs WKWebView embedding, not a guarantee for Mobile Safari or an installed home-screen PWA (which K7 is). This project's own Slideshow feature already faced this exact problem and deliberately chose a CSS-based in-place promotion instead (see the paired concept node) — any new fullscreen capability should follow that precedent rather than reopen the question.
---
