Decided 2026-09-14, resolving the manual-fullscreen-vs-Slideshow conflict: opening a card's manual fullscreen (via its header button) always suspends the Slideshow's own timers (idle-trigger and rotation-interval) for the duration, regardless of whether the Slideshow was already in its own fullscreen/rotating mode or still in normal "active" mode. Closing the manual fullscreen restores the Slideshow to whatever state it was in before the manual fullscreen opened: if the Slideshow was fullscreen and rotating, it resumes rotating (still fullscreen); if it was in normal active mode, the dashboard returns to normal paged view. The manual fullscreen takes priority for its duration; the Slideshow's own state underneath is paused, not reset or exited.
---
