Plan decision for k7-card-fullscreen: the existing Slideshow fullscreen mechanism (position:fixed class + .pager-track transform clear/restore + Pager.suspend/resume, previously inlined in slideshow.ts) is extracted into a new shared module, fullscreen-lock.ts, so the Slideshow and the new manual per-card trait both call through one ownership-aware controller instead of two independent implementations touching the same DOM class. Ownership is modeled as a pure, unit-tested reducer over {manualElId, slideshowWantsFullscreen} and four events (manual-acquire/manual-release/slideshow-enter/slideshow-exit): a manual acquire always takes the fullscreen slot; a manual release tears the promotion down only if the Slideshow no longer wants fullscreen — otherwise ownership just hands back to the Slideshow with the class left in place, matching the "closing the calendar leaves us with slideshow fullscreen, back with the slideshow slideshowing" rule. The CSS classes it now owns are renamed from k7-slideshow-active/k7-slideshow-veil to k7-fullscreen-active/k7-fullscreen-veil since they stop being Slideshow-exclusive (enter-fade/enter-slide stay Slideshow-only — the manual trait has no crossfade).
