Correction to the k7-card-fullscreen fullscreen-lock design (node 2733b7b2), caught by an independent /gw-plan-review pass on 2026-09-14 before implementation started: two points the original plan left as "decide during implementation" were actually settled facts, not open choices. (1) The promotion CSS class must be applied to the widget's custom-element host, never to Card.svelte's own `.card` element — app.css is a light-DOM stylesheet and Shadow DOM style encapsulation means it cannot match anything inside a shadow root, so the .card option was never technically viable. (2) The module extraction must cover slideshow.ts's rotate() (which does its own direct classList calls on every interval tick), not just enterFullscreen/exitFullscreen — otherwise a manual fullscreen acquired on a different card while the Slideshow is mid-rotation has no mechanism to depromote the Slideshow's card. Fixed by modeling the lock's pure state as {manualElId, slideshowElId} with a single derived promotedElId = manualElId ?? slideshowElId that the DOM-wiring half diffs on every event (manual-acquire/release, slideshow-enter/rotate/exit) rather than branching on a boolean "does the slideshow still want fullscreen" flag.
---
