Second correction to the k7-card-fullscreen fullscreen-lock design, caught by a second independent /gw-plan-review pass on 2026-09-14: the first fix (deriving promotedElId, routing rotate() through the lock) only covered slideshow.ts calling INTO fullscreen-lock.ts. It missed the reverse direction: slideshow.ts's own onInteraction (wired to window touchstart/mousedown/keydown) treats any interaction while its mode is 'fullscreen' as an exit signal (real config: pokaz-domowy sets exitOnInteraction:true and kalendarz is one of its cardIds). Composed touch/mouse events reach that window listener during the bubble phase before the new fullscreen button's own click handler runs, so tapping the button while the Slideshow is fullscreen-showing that card would fire the Slideshow's own exit path first, discarding slideshowElId entirely before the manual trait ever gets a chance to acquire the slot -- breaking the "resume slideshow after closing manual" rule (node ce2dbda2) for the exact scenario it was written for. Fixed by having onInteraction read the lock's manual-ownership state synchronously and return early (no reducer transition, no timer changes) whenever manual currently owns the slot, via a small pure helper shouldExitOnInteraction(mode, exitOnInteraction, manualOwned) unit-tested alongside slideshowReducer. This is the mirror image of Pager.suspend()/resume() (node c4b43952): that fixed the pager's touch listeners for this exact class of problem; onInteraction is a second, separate global listener the same problem applies to.
---
