-> DEPENDS_ON [node:ce2dbda2-1e9b-4f80-8757-871c05d6e031] @ 2026-09-14T20:52:06.070267+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-14T20:52:06.070267+00:00

Third and fourth corrections to the k7-card-fullscreen plan, caught by a third independent /gw-plan-review pass on 2026-09-14. (3) The onInteraction guard added in the previous fix (node 5797a5fc) checked manual-ownership at the wrong moment: real taps fire touchstart then touchend then synthetic mousedown then click, in that order, and slideshow.ts's window-level onInteraction listens for touchstart/mousedown -- both of which fire before click. Since Phase 2 had the button acquire fullscreen on click, onInteraction would see manualOwned still false on the very tap that acquires fullscreen, reproducing the defect the guard was meant to fix on its own demonstrating tap. Fixed by having the button acquire on touchstart/mousedown at the button element itself rather than click: DOM event dispatch runs target-phase listeners (bound on the element itself) before the same event reaches an ancestor's bubble-phase listener including window, so the button's own handler updates the lock's store before onInteraction ever sees that event. Releasing stays on click since manualOwned is already true for the whole viewing session by the time a closing tap occurs. (4) Node ce2dbda2 requires suspending the Slideshow's idle-trigger timer too, not just the rotation interval and the interaction guard -- nothing did. scheduleIdle()'s pending timeout kept running regardless of manual ownership, so a long dwell in manual fullscreen while the Slideshow was in its normal 'active' mode could let the idle timer fire underneath, silently flipping the Slideshow's internal mode to fullscreen (invisible while manual holds promotedElId) and corrupting what release falls back to. Fixed by giving the Slideshow controller its own suspend()/resume() pair (mirroring Pager.suspend()/resume()) that fullscreen-lock.ts's impure wiring calls at the same promotedElId null-transitions that already drive the pager/transform handling.
---
