-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-14T20:57:29.815032+00:00

Fifth correction to the k7-card-fullscreen plan, caught by a fourth independent /gw-plan-review pass on 2026-09-14. The prior fix (node aa09008b) gave the Slideshow controller its own suspend()/resume() pair but wired it to fire on the same promotedElId (= manualElId ?? slideshowElId) null-transitions that correctly drive the pager/track-transform handling. That trigger is wrong for the Slideshow's own timers specifically: manual acquiring the SAME card the Slideshow already has fullscreen-promoted produces no change in promotedElId at all (still the same value), and manual acquiring a DIFFERENT card while the Slideshow is rotating produces a non-null-to-non-null transition, not a null-crossing -- in both cases (exactly the two scenarios the coordination rule ce2dbda2 and the plan's own Phase 3 scenarios 3/4 exist to cover) the Slideshow's interval timer would keep silently ticking underneath, state.index advancing, with the drift only surfacing later when release lands on the wrong card. Fixed by keying slideshow.suspend()/resume() to manualElId's OWN null-transitions instead: every manual-acquire event calls suspend() (regardless of what promotedElId was doing), every manual-release event calls resume(). This is a genuinely different trigger condition from the pager/track handling, not the same symmetry the previous fix assumed. Phase 3's scenarios 3 and 4 were also extended to require a dwell longer than intervalSeconds before checking release behavior, since without that the manual verification could pass by accident (no visible symptom while the interval silently advances in the background).
