Phase 1 implementation decisions for k7-card-fullscreen, resolving two details the plan left slightly underspecified. (1) onInteraction computes manualOwned = isManualFullscreenActive() once at the top, then gates BOTH branches with it: the 'active'-mode branch inlines `if (!manualOwned) scheduleIdle()` directly (manual owning the slot must not silently undo the idle-timer suspension from Slideshow.suspend()), while the 'fullscreen'-mode branch passes manualOwned into the pure shouldExitOnInteraction(mode, exitOnInteraction, manualOwned) helper. Both branches needed the guard, not just the fullscreen one, since a repeated tap inside a manually-fullscreened card would otherwise reschedule the idle timer via the active branch even though suspend() had already cleared it. (2) fullscreenLockReducer's manual-release event carries elId (matching the plan's releaseManual(elId) signature) and only clears manualElId when it equals the event's elId, otherwise the event is a no-op -- a defensive guard so a stale/late release call can never clobber a newer acquire, even though with only one fullscreen-enabled widget today (Calendar) this can't yet occur in practice; the API is designed for future multi-widget adoption.
---
