Phase 2 implementation discovery for k7-card-fullscreen: Card.svelte's own `state` prop (ok/warn/fail/idle) collides with the `$state` rune the same way K7Calendar.svelte's existing code comments already document -- a local binding literally named `state` turns every `$state(...)` call in the file into Svelte's store-subscription syntax, and the compiler error blames the rune call site, not the name. This is the first time it bit Card.svelte itself (the shared shell every widget's own feature might eventually touch), not just a single widget. Fixed by renaming the destructured local binding to `cardStatus` (the Props interface and prop name callers pass stay `state`, so no call site elsewhere needed updating) -- worth remembering before any future Card.svelte feature reaches for $state.
---
