Second real bug found only via real-browser testing during k7-card-fullscreen Phase 3, discovered after the first fix (node 2b7b465d) via a genuine scenario-3 test failure (not a test artifact -- traced with instrumented state logging to confirm): a card's fullscreen button must distinguish "is this card fullscreen at all" from "does MANUAL specifically own this card's fullscreen slot" -- they are not the same thing, since the Slideshow can independently promote the same card. The pointerdown handler's "already fullscreen, defer to click" branch was gated on the generic isFullscreen (promotedElId === hostId), which is also true when the Slideshow currently shows this exact card with no manual acquire having happened yet. Tapping the button in that state took the "already handled, do nothing" branch instead of acquiring -- so the mousedown bubbled to window with manual ownership still false, and slideshow.ts's own exit-on-interaction guard (correctly, from its own perspective) read this as an ordinary interaction and exited the Slideshow's fullscreen entirely, clearing slideshowElId before the household ever got a chance to take manual control of the card the Slideshow was already showing. Fixed by exposing manualElIdStore (parallel to promotedElIdStore) from fullscreen-lock.ts, and gating the button's pointerdown/click logic on isManuallyMine (manualElIdStore === hostId) instead of the generic isFullscreen: only "I already manually hold this" defers to click for release; "not fullscreen at all" and "the Slideshow put me here" both acquire immediately on pointerdown, winning the same race the first fix already solved for the plain not-fullscreen case.
---
