CalendarEvent's current definition ("An entry in the household Google calendar... that difference is what forces OAuth2 rather than a public .ics") is too narrow now that the Calendar entity exists (k7-multi-calendar, 2026-09-15, human-approved): it assumes a single, always-editable, Google-only source. Proposed broadened wording, approved by the human but not written into the entity itself (per this project's domain-editing discipline -- an entity's definition is never silently overwritten): "An entry belonging to a Calendar. Whether it can be added/edited/deleted depends on its Calendar's source -- the household's Google calendar is read-write, an .ics-sourced Calendar is read-only." Whether to actually update the stored definition text is the human's own action in the memory GUI's Domain tab; this artifact and the CONTRADICTED event on CalendarEvent exist so the correction is visible at every future recall regardless of whether the text itself changes.
