node-ical (v0.27.x, ~1.1M downloads/month, depends on rrule-temporal for RRULE/recurring-event expansion) is the candidate library for parsing .ics feeds in k7-multi-calendar, matching this project's precedent of picking a mature, actively-maintained parser for a new upstream format rather than hand-rolling one (rss-parser for comic-of-the-day's RSS/Atom). Recurring events (RRULE) matter here specifically because the motivating use case -- a school schedule -- is exactly the kind of feed built almost entirely from weekly-recurring events. No existing ics/ical dependency exists in package.json today. The design system has no existing tabs UI pattern anywhere (checked DESIGN.md and the component kit) -- this is genuinely new surface, unlike the fullscreen button which could reuse the shell header's existing ghost-button/bracket-glyph recipe directly.
