Plan decision for k7-multi-calendar: each configured Calendar is fetched independently (its own HTTP/API request, its own freshness-cache key and entry), rather than one combined request/cache-row for the whole card. This is a new pattern for this codebase -- every existing multi-source card (weather, comics) has exactly one upstream per card. Chosen so one dead .ics feed (a school's system down) doesn't blank the whole calendar card or block other calendars' events from showing; each source fails independently and falls back to its own last-good cache or, for Google with no credentials configured, the existing mock-event fallback. Structured configuration (the calendars array, each with a nested source object) is passed from main.ts's createWidget to the k7-calendar custom element as a single JSON.stringify'd attribute, parsed back out in K7Calendar.svelte -- a new technique for this codebase (existing complex-param cards like timer flatten to a comma-joined string, insufficient for genuinely nested per-item objects).
