Wireframe decision for k7-multi-calendar's tab strip: touch handling is native overflow-x scroll on the strip itself, with the strip's own touchstart/touchmove handlers calling stopPropagation() so a horizontal tab-scroll gesture can never also register as a page-swipe on the ancestor Pager -- reusing the interference-avoidance reasoning K7Carousel.svelte's own docstring already establishes for the identical class of problem (a nested touch surface competing with the page-level pager), not its discrete slide-snap math (tabs are independently-tappable variable-width buttons, not full-width slides to snap between).
