-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-15T08:33:47.970335+00:00

Wireframe decision for k7-multi-calendar's per-calendar colour ticks: colours are computed dynamically (evenly-spaced hue around the wheel, avoiding the reserved semantic hues -- warn/fail/amber-ink/signal -- same "hue separation has to be earned" reasoning as WARNNOTAMBER's own hue-27/45/72 spacing) rather than drawn from a small fixed set of named tokens, because the number of calendars a household configures is arbitrary and unknown at theme-build time -- a fixed palette would either run out (too many calendars) or be needlessly coarse (too few, when finer even spacing would look more distinct). The math runs in JavaScript, not CSS -- this project bans Safari-15-incompatible CSS colour functions (oklch()/color-mix() in OUTPUT css) but that constraint is about what ships in .css files, not about doing colour math in TS and writing the RESULT out as a plain hex string via an inline custom-property value. This is a deliberate, reasoned exception to "components read only var(--*) tokens" (TOKENCONTRACT), not a violation of it -- the value is still derived programmatically using this project's own colour-space reasoning, just computed per-request based on runtime cardinality (calendars.length) instead of baked into the static build-time token sheet. Left open for implementation: exact lightness/chroma tuning to clear the 3:1 border-contrast floor across all three luminance modes (light/dark/night) needs real contrast-checking during implementation, not guessed at here.
---
