k7-multi-calendar Phase 1 implementation decision: `Calendar`/`CalendarSource` types live in `src/server/domain/types.ts` only, not duplicated into the client's `calendar.ts` in this phase. Reasoning: domain/types.ts already houses Upstream (the cross-cutting enum the calendar upstream fetchers key off), and Phase 2/3's ics-calendar.ts/google-calendar.ts need CalendarSource server-side to route fetch-by-mode; there is no existing precedent anywhere in this codebase for client importing server types (checked: no `from '.../server` import in src/client/), so a client-side Calendar/CalendarSource declaration, if needed, is deferred to Phase 4 (which already modifies calendar.ts to add CalendarEvent.calendarId) rather than introduced speculatively now. CalendarEvent itself stays client-only per existing precedent; server upstream modules (open-meteo.ts, etc.) define their own local response shapes rather than importing from domain/types.ts, so Phase 2/3's ics/google fetchers will follow that same convention for their CalendarEvent-shaped output.
