Plan gap found during k7-multi-calendar Phase 2 (not blocking Phase 2 itself, flagging for Phase 4): no phase in plan.md lists src/server/index.ts as a file to modify, yet /api/calendar/week has never existed as a real route (confirmed in research.md's [node:156c9e97] finding) and none of Phases 2/3/4/5 currently wire ics-calendar.ts or google-calendar.ts's fetchers into an actual HTTP route via fetchThrough, the way index.ts already does for /api/comic and the weather route. Phase 4's stated file list (K7Calendar.svelte, calendar.ts, main.ts) has nowhere to route a real per-calendar fetch to. This needs an explicit addition to Phase 4 (or a new Phase 4 bullet) adding a real /api/calendar/week route in src/server/index.ts that dispatches to fetchIcsCalendar or fetchGoogleCalendar by source.mode, wrapped in fetchThrough with the appropriate cache key (icsCacheKey/google-calendar equivalent) — otherwise Phase 4's frontend work has no real backend to call and the feature silently stays mocked end-to-end.
