-> HAS_FACET [node:956d5165-5c27-4183-a5e2-c077d213f32a] @ 2026-09-15T11:09:51.444607+00:00

k7-multi-calendar Phase 3 implementation decisions for src/server/upstream/google-calendar.ts: (1) Consolidated the server-side CalendarEvent shape into domain/types.ts (moved out of ics-calendar.ts, which originally declared it locally as IcsCalendarEvent) since Phase 3 needs the identical shape — this is the first case in the codebase of two upstream modules (ics-calendar.ts, google-calendar.ts) producing the same domain concept, unlike every other upstream which is the sole source of its own shape. (2) hasGoogleCalendarCredentials(creds) is a plain boundary type-guard the caller uses to decide whether to invoke this module at all — absent credentials never reaches requestAccessToken/fetchEvents, which both assume valid creds (trust internal invariants, validate only at the boundary). This is how "absent credentials falls back to the client's existing mock display" gets implemented: the future route simply skips calling this module and lets the request fail the same way it does today (no route at all), rather than this module manufacturing a fallback. (3) Access-token caching is closure-scoped per createGoogleCalendarClient() instance, not a bare module-level global — functionally equivalent given this project's own precedent (kilo.ts's createKiloGatewayClient) of constructing upstream clients once at boot and reusing them for the process lifetime, but closure-scoping makes it trivially testable (each test constructs its own client) without cross-test cache pollution. Token refreshed 60s before its stated expiry (EXPIRY_SAFETY_MARGIN_SECONDS) so an in-flight request never starts with a token that expires mid-call. (4) Google's events.list is queried with singleEvents=true&orderBy=startTime, which makes Google itself expand recurring events into instances server-side — unlike the .ics path (Phase 2), there is no client-side RRULE expansion needed for the Google source. Cancelled instances (status: 'cancelled') are dropped in mapGoogleEvent, not shown as events.
