k7-multi-calendar (merged as PR #45, mt3o/kitchen-terminal-k7, commit 74bc85b on main): the calendar card now supports any number of configured calendars — the household's existing Google account plus any number of read-only .ics feeds (motivating case: a kid's school schedule) — each fetched independently through a new GET /api/calendar/week route so one dead feed never blanks the others. A tab strip (built against an agreed wireframe deck, context/design/k7-calendar-card/deck.json) appears once there is more than one calendar; a GŁÓWNY tab merges every calendar flagged showInMain, any other tab shows just that one calendar regardless of its own flag. A single configured calendar (today's real household setup) renders pixel-identical to the pre-multi-calendar card. Google OAuth2 was deliberately bounded to a refresh-token exchange + read-only events.list — no consent-flow UI exists or was built. Three degraded states are distinguished per calendar: not-configured (Google, no credentials — falls back to the pre-existing mock-event display), stale (cache available, [!] glyph), no-cache (synthetic all-day error placeholders, [X] glyph) — the card's footer badge/meta aggregate worst-case across ALL configured calendars regardless of showInMain, by deliberate design. Real-browser verified against a real public .ics feed (Google's published US-holidays calendar) before merge; the colour-tick hue/contrast was verified numerically against the real theme tokens, not guessed. One pre-existing (not introduced by this change) reactivity bug was found during review and filed separately, not fixed here: K7Calendar.svelte's day-column labels freeze after the first week rollover on a long-running kiosk.
