-> HAS_FACET [node:d40736ae-86f3-4437-b0dd-4f36ae159f42] @ 2026-09-15T12:53:23.002143+00:00

Change summary / gw-review verdict for k7-calendar-ssrf-fix: Approve. The fix genuinely closes the /api/calendar/week SSRF — the route now reads only `id` from req.query (src/server/index.ts), resolves mode+url/calendarId exclusively from layout.yaml via findConfiguredCalendar() (src/server/calendar-lookup.ts), and the two fetch call sites (fetchIcsCalendar, googleCalendarClient.fetchEvents) receive only values traced back to that lookup — no remaining client-controlled query/body/header reaches either fetch. findConfiguredCalendar's recursive search over grid cells + carousel slides was verified correct against the actual runtime Card/Layout/NormalisedLayout types in src/shared/layout.ts and against src/client/main.ts's buildNestedChild (cells/slides keys match exactly). The schema (docs/handoff/layout.schema.yaml) also allows a card inside sidebar.content, which findConfiguredCalendar does not search — but this is not a gap introduced by this PR: sidebar is not represented at all in the narrower runtime Layout/Card/NormalisedLayout types (src/shared/layout.ts) or in normaliseLayout(), so a sidebar-nested calendar could not reach the route regardless; findConfiguredCalendar simply fails closed (404) rather than reintroducing the vuln. test/calendar-lookup.test.ts's 6 tests exercise the lookup's recursive-search correctness and its fail-closed behavior on an unconfigured id well, though they are unit tests of findConfiguredCalendar only — there is no route-level (fastify .inject) regression test proving the live endpoint now ignores mode/url/calendarId if a client still sends them; this is a reasonable call given index.ts boots the whole server as an import side effect (per the module's own doc comment) and is not the pattern used for other still-inline routes, but chat.ts's registerChatRoutes extraction + chat-routes.test.ts shows the project does have a precedent for the stronger route-level test where a route is worth extracting. Also fixed: K7Calendar.svelte's stale day-label reactivity bug (days := weekDays(weekStart) -> $derived(weekDays(weekStart))), a genuine unrelated fix, user-facing.
---
