Found during k7-calendar-ssrf-fix's review, out of scope for that PR: /api/comic (src/server/index.ts ~line 297) has the same class of SSRF /api/calendar/week just had. It reads a client-supplied `rssUrl` query param directly and passes it unvalidated into fetchComic() -> fetchWithTimeout(query.rssUrl, ...) (src/server/upstream/comic-rss.ts, fetchComic ~line 70) — no scheme check, no isPrivateAddress() guard, unlike src/server/recipes/import.ts's assertImportable() which already does exactly this validation for recipe URL imports. A LAN client can therefore direct K7's server to fetch an arbitrary internal address via GET /api/comic?rssUrl=http://127.0.0.1:PORT/.... Needs its own fix: either resolve rssUrl server-side from layout.yaml's configured comic-of-the-day card (matching the calendar fix's pattern) or, if rssUrl must stay client-configurable per the layout schema's design, apply the same host/scheme guard recipes/import.ts already has (isPrivateAddress in src/server/security/network.ts).
