retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:bb5beeed-3cc4-468a-b4c3-a6575cb25f41] @ 2026-09-15T12:53:39.376790+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c3dc31be-39b3-4422-a4f6-41136bfb48aa] @ 2026-09-15T12:53:39.376790+00:00

Lesson from k7-calendar-ssrf-fix's review, for every future route added to src/server/index.ts: any req.query/req.body field that is, or is used to build, a URL fetched server-side is an SSRF vector by default and must be closed one of two ways — (a) resolved server-side from layout.yaml (trusted, household-edited only) rather than accepted from the request, the pattern this change established via findConfiguredCalendar()/calendar-lookup.ts, or (b) validated with the existing isPrivateAddress()/scheme-allowlist guard in src/server/security/network.ts before any fetch, the pattern src/server/recipes/import.ts's assertImportable() already uses. Neither guard is applied uniformly today — a grep for req.query at review time found /api/comic's rssUrl still unguarded (see the paired issue node) — so this constraint is not yet enforced by any lint/test and should be checked by hand on every new or touched route until it is.
---
