-> HAS_FACET [node:c3dc31be-39b3-4422-a4f6-41136bfb48aa] @ 2026-09-15T12:57:03.955270+00:00

Extended k7-calendar-ssrf-fix beyond the original PR scope: /gw-review flagged that /api/comic's rssUrl query param has the identical SSRF vulnerability (client-supplied URL fetched server-side with zero validation) — live and unpatched at review time, captured by the reviewer as [node:fb0cacd3] issue + [node:87702f1f] generalizing constraint. Fixed in the same PR rather than deferred: extracted the guard logic (scheme allowlist + isPrivateAddress check) that recipes/import.ts's assertImportable already had into a new shared isFetchableUrl(url: URL): boolean in src/server/security/network.ts, refactored recipes/import.ts to use it (behavior-preserving, no test depended on the old two-branch error message), and applied it to /api/comic's rssUrl before fetching. New test/network-fetchable-url.test.ts covers the shared guard directly. Deliberately did NOT apply this guard to the .ics calendar fetch (now resolved from layout.yaml, trusted config — a household member pointing an .ics calendar at an internal address is a legitimate choice, not an attack, unlike a value arriving in a request).
