k7-calendar-ssrf-fix (merged as PR #47, mt3o/kitchen-terminal-k7, commit 13b20a3 on main): fixed a real, live SSRF vulnerability in /api/calendar/week — it trusted client-supplied mode/url/calendarId and fetched url server-side with zero validation, found during k7-multi-calendar's own deployment by the peer session on the home server. The route now takes only id; the real source is resolved server-side from layout.yaml via a new pure findConfiguredCalendar() (src/server/calendar-lookup.ts), searched recursively through grid cells and carousel slides. During /gw-review, the same vulnerability class was found still live in /api/comic's rssUrl and fixed in the same PR: a shared isFetchableUrl() guard (scheme allowlist + private-address check) was extracted into src/server/security/network.ts from recipes/import.ts's pre-existing assertImportable, and applied to both call sites. Also fixed K7Calendar.svelte's pre-existing days/weekStart reactivity bug, flagged independently by this project's own review and the deploy check. Two independent adversarial reviews (one from a fresh /gw-review agent, one implicitly from the peer session's own deploy-time scrutiny) both found real issues that got fixed before this shipped.
